  "ingredients": [
    "1 teaspoon unsalted butter, or as needed",
    "2 large eggs",
    "0.25 teaspoon white vinegar",
    "1 pinch salt"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Line a baking sheet with a silicone liner (such as Silpat); lightly butter.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Separate egg whites and egg yolks. Place whites in a large bowl. Reserve yolks in two separate, smaller bowls.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Add vinegar to egg whites then add salt; whisk until reaches relatively firm, but not dry, peaks.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Spoon egg whites onto the prepared baking sheet, shape as desired, making sure not too wide, since want some height. Make a small depression in centers using the back of a spoon.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in center of the preheated oven until egg whites just start to take on some golden color, 5 to 6 minutes. Add yolks to depressions; bake until yolks are heated through, but still runny, 3 to 4 minutes more.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
